      "topicNote": "Moved to Circles, Arcs & Sectors.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Let the side length",
          "body": "Let the side length of the square be \\(s\\)."
        },
        {
          "title": "Square",
          "body": "The circle is inscribed in the square, so its radius is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{s}{2}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "The shaded area is the",
          "body": "The shaded area is the area of the square minus the area of the circle:\n\n\\[\ns^2-\\pi\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)^2=80\n\\]\n\n\\[\ns^2-\\frac{\\pi s^2}{4}=80\n\\]\n\n\\[\ns^2\\left(1-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=80\n\\]\n\n\\[\ns=\\sqrt{\\frac{80}{1-\\frac{\\pi}{4}}}=19.3076\\ldots\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "The diagonal of the square",
          "body": "The diagonal of the square is\n\n\\[\nAC=s\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nAC=19.3076\\ldots\\sqrt{2}=27.3051\\ldots\n\\]"
